    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="32.2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 32.2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="32.2" corresp="#wit-d-incomplete">And gemeta ⁊ gewihta rihte man georne, ⁊ ælces unrihtes heonan forð geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="32.2" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ gemeta ⁊ gewihta rihte man georne, ⁊ ælces unrihtes heonan forð geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And gemeta and gewihta rihte man georne, and ælces unrihtes heonan forð geswice.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And weights and measures shall be corrected with all diligence, and an end put to all unjust practices.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And weights and measures are to be assiduously made right, and all unlawful practices abolished henceforth.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und Maasse und Gewichte mache man genau richtig, und lasse hinfort von jedem Unrechte ab.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let measures and weights be carefully corrected, and let all injustice cease henceforth.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="255"><ref target="clause:IIIEg_8-1">III Eg 8.1</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 8, 1</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:IICn_9">II Cn 9</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#whitelock" n="463"><ref target="clause:IICn_8-2">II Cn 8.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="358"><ref target="clause:IICn_9">II Cn 9</ref></note>
      </div>
